  "worked_solution": "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x=-\\frac{7}{3}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(-\\frac{7}{3})=-(66.801\\,4\u2026)^{\u2218}\u2248-{66.801}^{\u2218}\n$$\n\nSince $-{66.801}^{\u2218}$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{\u2218}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={180}^{\u2218}+x \\\\  & ={180}^{\u2218}+(-{66.801}^{\u2218}) \\\\  & =113.199 \\\\  & \u2248{113}^{\u2218}, \\\\ {x}_{2} & =2\\cdot {180}^{\u2218}+x \\\\  & ={360}^{\u2218}+(-{66.801}^{\u2218}) \\\\  & =293.199 \\\\  & \u2248{293}^{\u2218},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\neach rounded to the nearest integer.\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x={113}^{\u2218}$ and $x={293}^{\u2218}.$",
